      "code": "if (memcmp (battr->timecode, cattr->timecode, sizeof(exr_attr_timecode_t)))",
      "role": "sink",
      "note": "memcmp dereferences battr->timecode which is actually the inline POD union bytes interpreted as a pointer. Since the union was zero-initialized except for the single compression byte, this pointer is NULL or a tiny address, causing an invalid memory read and segfault."
